import io

PATH = "E:/Archive/GitHub/dlandi/LimboDancer.MCP/src/ASL/docs/Prompts/Pass Standing Rules and Harness Lessons.md"
s = io.open(PATH, encoding="utf-8", newline="").read()
assert s.endswith("\n") and "\r\n" not in s

A = "- **A fix gets a small test game and its tests** (the user, 2026-10-09). When a rule pass builds as it goes, each fix is shown in the Studio in a game of a few counters made for it, and has a Rules test and, where the planner writes events, a Play test. Say plainly when a fix has no game and why.\n"
B = A + '''- **The Studio game is not skipped for cost** (the user, 2026-10-09). "No game" is for what cannot be staged, such as terrain the board lacks; an exception for any other reason is the user's to give. In pass 35 the games found five faults the tests had passed: a page that did not offer an allowed action, a check that refused before the repaired rule was read, a repair that reached one case too many, a stale selection in a panel, and a game file that carried played events.
- **Search the whole rulebook before saying what a counter or a rule needs** (the user, 2026-10-09). A counter's rules are spread through the book by cross-reference. Scan every page of the PDF for the word (PyMuPDF; the nearest rule number above each mention), compare with the inventory's rows, and say which rules were read on their page and which are only where the word stands. The script of the first such scan is `E:/Archive/GitHub/dlandi/pass32-tools/pass35/counter_scan.py`; the backlog's section 55.1 has its result.
'''
assert s.count(A) == 1
s = s.replace(A, B)

s += '''- **More of the test game's recipe (pass 35, second session).** A Gun in tow is created with `holding` (`holder` the vehicle, `role` "towed"), no position, and empty conditions; a Passenger with `position` `{"in": <vehicle>, "role": "passenger"}`; a LATW is `kind` "asl:latw" with `role` "possessed". Conditions a counter may start with: `asl:motion`, `asl:bogged`, `asl:recalled` with `asl:stun-recovery` (a Recalled AFV that must leave), `asl:bu` false (a CT AFV with its crew exposed), `asl:bounding-fire`, `asl:cc-reaction`. Night and weather are `specialRules` of `game-started`: `night:<NVR>`, `weather:mud`. The other side moves first when `phasingSide` of `game-started` and of every `phase-changed` names it. Never build a game from one that has been played: it carries the played events and does not replay; take the `game-started` payload only. Setup refuses a vehicle beside an enemy unit, but a file may place one. Keep the generator scripts outside the scratchpad, which is lost with the session.
- **Board 3, more (pass 35, second session):** a road runs [D5], [E6], [F6]; the woods of [F5] are Bypassed from [E6] beside [F6]; from [D9] a vehicle facing south-east enters [D10] or [E10], and facing south-west [D10] or [C10], all Open Ground; [O3] has its wall toward [P3] and [O4]; a Recalled vehicle's route off the left edge is decided from [D10] and west of it, not from [E10] or [P10]. No rubble, hedge, unpaved road through other terrain, or road through a wall is known on it.
- **Driving the Play page, more:** the vehicle panel is `#vehicle-unit`, then a button a step, found by its text ("enter bd03:D10:0", "start in Reverse", "resolve the OVR"), with `#vehicle-ovr`, `#vehicle-stop`, `#vehicle-unbog`, `#vehicle-esb-mp` and `#vehicle-esb`, `.vehicle-unload` and `#vehicle-unload`, and `.bu-toggle[data-vehicle]`; a disabled step's `title` is its refusal. Ordnance is `#ordnance-gun`, `#ordnance-target`, `#ordnance-vehicle`, `#propose-ordnance`; fire is `#fire-from`, `.fire-firer` (by index: they carry no value), `#fire-target`, `#propose-fire`; Infantry Bypass is `.move-unit`, `#move-to`, `#move-bypass` ("south"), `#propose-move`; the DEFENDER passes with `#propose-pass`, a move ends with `#propose-end-move`. Close Combat with a vehicle has its own panel: `.vehicle-cc[data-location]` with `.vehicle-cc-vehicle`, `.vehicle-cc-defender`, `.propose-vehicle-cc-vehicle`, `.propose-vehicle-cc-pass`; one Location at a time, the Infantry side first. A vehicle that has moved must Stop, the DEFENDER pass, the move end, and the DEFENDER pass again before another vehicle moves. The page lags a commit: wait four seconds and read the lists again before trusting them.
- **Read a record from the game file, not from the page:** the "Latest" line leaves out the DRM. The file in `boards/units/live/.../<id>.game.json` has each `fire-resolved`, `ordnance-fired`, and `vehicle-close-combat-resolved` with its `resolution` (`arithmetic.drm`, `totalFirepower`, `defending[].finalDr`).
- **Claude's Studio of the last session may still be running** on 6671 and hold `bin/p31b`: list the `dotnet` processes with their command lines, and stop the one that runs the MapStudio DLL of `bin/p31b` on 6671 before the first build.
- **Shell, more:** never put Markdown with backticks inside a double-quoted shell string: the shell runs each span as a command and writes the text without it (2026-10-09; nothing real ran, the file was restored). Write such text with the Write tool into a script file. Printing PDF text from Python needs `PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8`. A test file with a one-line `with { ... }` fails IDE0055 and is fixed by `dotnet format whitespace <csproj> --include <file>`. A positional record gains a fact as a trailing parameter with a default, or as an `init` property with `JsonIgnore` when null, so recorded games keep their shape.
'''
io.open(PATH, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="").write(s)
print("ok")
